{"id":"R010","inputs":["H001","H002","N005","N006","N007","N008","N009"],"output":"N010","definitions":["D003","D004","D007","D013","D014","D015","D016","D019","D020"],"rules":["direct","forall_introduction","implication_introduction","case_elimination"],"locals":[{"symbol":"u","type":"smooth real mean-zero solution path","scope":"R010/argument","start":"S001","end":"S004","kind":"arbitrary","declaration":"Fix any smooth real mean-zero u on [0,T] satisfying u_t+u_xxx=(1/2)*partial_x(u^2), the normalized KdV equation in D020.","from_inputs":[],"from_local":[],"objects":["T","KdV"]},{"symbol":"v","type":"smooth real mean-zero twisted path","scope":"R010/argument","start":"S001","end":"S004","kind":"definition","declaration":"Define v(t)=S_(-t)u(t) for the fixed normalized exact solution u.","from_inputs":[],"from_local":[],"objects":["S","u"]},{"symbol":"V","type":"continuous numerical interpolation","scope":"R010/argument","start":"S001","end":"S004","kind":"definition","declaration":"Take the interpolation of the fixed scheme initialized by v(0).","from_inputs":["N007"],"from_local":[],"objects":["v","Interp"]},{"symbol":"Rres","type":"actual concatenated residual","scope":"R010/argument","start":"S001","end":"S004","kind":"definition","declaration":"Take the residual of this interpolation.","from_inputs":["N007"],"from_local":[],"objects":["Interp","V"]},{"symbol":"M","type":"exact norm bound","scope":"R010/argument","start":"S001","end":"S004","kind":"definition","declaration":"Define M=1+sup_[0,T]||v||_(H^gamma).","from_inputs":["H001","H002"],"from_local":[],"objects":["T","gamma","v","H"]},{"symbol":"e","type":"continuous error path","scope":"R010/argument","start":"S001","end":"S004","kind":"definition","declaration":"Define e=v-V.","from_inputs":[],"from_local":[],"objects":["v","V"]},{"symbol":"tau","type":"positive timestep","scope":"R010/argument","start":"S001","end":"S004","kind":"arbitrary","declaration":"Fix 0<tau<=1.","from_inputs":[],"from_local":[],"objects":[]},{"symbol":"I","type":"closed interval","scope":"R010/argument","start":"S001","end":"S004","kind":"arbitrary","declaration":"Fix I=[a,b] subset [0,T], starting at a grid point.","from_inputs":[],"from_local":[],"objects":[]},{"symbol":"a","type":"grid left endpoint","scope":"R010/argument","start":"S001","end":"S004","kind":"arbitrary","declaration":"Let a be the left endpoint.","from_inputs":[],"from_local":[],"objects":[]},{"symbol":"b","type":"right endpoint","scope":"R010/argument","start":"S001","end":"S004","kind":"arbitrary","declaration":"Let b be the right endpoint.","from_inputs":[],"from_local":[],"objects":[]},{"symbol":"h","type":"interval length","scope":"R010/argument","start":"S001","end":"S004","kind":"definition","declaration":"Define h=b-a<=1.","from_inputs":[],"from_local":[],"objects":["a","b"]},{"symbol":"E_I","type":"error supremum","scope":"R010/argument","start":"S001","end":"S004","kind":"definition","declaration":"Define E_I=sup_I||e||_2.","from_inputs":[],"from_local":[],"objects":["I","e","H"]},{"symbol":"N","type":"real threshold","scope":"R010/argument","start":"S002","end":"S004","kind":"arbitrary","declaration":"Fix arbitrary N>=2.","from_inputs":[],"from_local":[],"objects":[]},{"symbol":"FI","type":"bilinear error integral","scope":"R010/argument","start":"S002","end":"S004","kind":"definition","declaration":"Define FI(t)=integral_a^t B_s(e,v-e/2)ds.","from_inputs":[],"from_local":[],"objects":["a","e","v","B"]},{"symbol":"g","type":"smooth comparison path","scope":"R010/argument","start":"S002","end":"S004","kind":"definition","declaration":"Define g=v-e/2.","from_inputs":[],"from_local":[],"objects":["v","e"]},{"symbol":"f1","type":"path of finite X norm on I","scope":"R010/argument","start":"S003","end":"S003","kind":"arbitrary","declaration":"Fix arbitrary f1 in X(I) for the projection estimate.","objects":[],"from_inputs":[],"from_local":[]},{"symbol":"f2","type":"path of finite X norm on I","scope":"R010/argument","start":"S003","end":"S003","kind":"arbitrary","declaration":"Fix arbitrary f2 in X(I) for the projection estimate.","objects":[],"from_inputs":[],"from_local":[]},{"symbol":"f3","type":"path of finite X norm on I","scope":"R010/argument","start":"S003","end":"S003","kind":"arbitrary","declaration":"Fix arbitrary f3 in X(I) for the projection estimate.","objects":[],"from_inputs":[],"from_local":[]}],"argument":[{"id":"S001","text":"Fix any smooth real mean-zero solution u of u_t+u_xxx=(1/2)*partial_x(u^2) on [0,T], the normalized KdV equation of D020, and define v(t)=S_(-t)u(t). Take its numerical interpolation V with residual Rres. Put M=1+sup||v||_(H^gamma), e=v-V and fix I=[a,b] starting at a grid point, h=b-a<=1, 0<tau<=1. Assume L1: E_I=sup_I||e||_2<=1. At each step intersecting I use f=v^n=V(t_n), w=v(t_n), delta_n=||f-w||_2<=E_I and q_n=tau^gamma+delta_n. N007 supplies the actual residual identity and grid values, and N009 gives sup||rho_n||_2<=C_M tau q_n and ||Rres'||_(L^infty H^(-p_star))<=C_M q_n. There are at most h/tau+1 intersected steps (including a final partial step). Hence sup_(a<=t<=b)||Rres(t)-Rres(a)||_2<=C_M(h+tau)(tau^gamma+E_I). For the exact path, D004 gives partial_t S_(-t)=partial_x^3 S_(-t), commuting with spatial derivatives. Thus v'=S_(-t)(u_t+u_xxx)=(1/2)S_(-t)partial_x(u^2)=(1/2)B_t(v,v), since S_t v=u. Smoothness justifies this differentiation and the spatial products. Subtracting N007's identity V'=B_t(V,V)/2+Rres' and using symmetry and bilinearity gives e'=(B_t(v,v)-B_t(V,V))/2-Rres'=B_t(e,(v+V)/2)-Rres'=B_t(e,v-e/2)-Rres'. N005 then gives ||e||_X(I)<=C_M(tau^gamma+E_I), and ||v||_X(I)+||V||_X(I)<=C_M. Here V=v-e, and the exact solution has L2 norm <=M throughout.","uses":["H001","H002","N005","N007","N009"],"uses_local":[],"objects":["T","gamma","v","V","Rres","M","e","I","a","b","h","tau","E_I","H","B","X","Interp","u","S","KdV"],"produces":[{"id":"F001","statement":"sup_I||Rres(t)-Rres(a)||_2<=C_M(h+tau)(tau^gamma+E_I), ||e||_X(I)<=C_M(tau^gamma+E_I), and ||v||_X(I)+||V||_X(I)<=C_M.","binders":[],"objects":["M","h","tau","gamma","E_I","Rres","a","e","v","V","I","H","X"],"assumptions":["L1"]}],"introduces":["L1"],"discharges":[]},{"id":"S002","text":"Define FI(t)=integral_a^t B_s(e,v-e/2)ds. Integration gives e(t)=e(a)+FI(t)-(Rres(t)-Rres(a)). Fix N>=2 only for analysis. For low frequencies N005's bound ||Dinv P(FG)||_2<=C||F||_2||G||_2, followed by two powers of frequency on |k|<=N, gives sup_I||P_(<=N)FI||_2<=C_M N^2 h E_I. For high frequencies apply the normal form in N005 with g=v-e/2, retaining both endpoints. Since e'=B(e,g)-Rres' and g'=B(v,v)/2-B(e,g)/2+Rres'/2, symmetry of J and the cubic identity give exactly FI(t)=[J_s(e,g)]_a^t/3-Cint_[a,t](e,g,V)/3-Cint_[a,t](v,v,e)/6+(1/3)integral_a^t J_s(Rres',V)ds. Indeed g-e/2=V combines the first differentiated pair, and -J(Rres',g)+J(e,Rres')/2=-J(Rres',V) before multiplication by -1/3. N005's H^1 bound on J bounds both high-output endpoints by C_M N^(-1)E_I. This includes the initial endpoint when e(a)!=0.","uses":["N005"],"uses_local":["F001"],"objects":["v","V","Rres","M","e","I","a","b","h","tau","E_I","N","FI","g","H","Dinv","B","J","Cint"],"produces":[{"id":"F002","statement":"e(t)=e(a)+FI(t)-(Rres(t)-Rres(a)); sup_I||P_(<=N)FI||_2<=C_M N^2 h E_I; FI(t)=[J_s(e,g)]_a^t/3-Cint_[a,t](e,g,V)/3-Cint_[a,t](v,v,e)/6+(1/3)integral_a^t J_s(Rres',V)ds, with g=v-e/2, and the high-output endpoint norm is <=C_M N^(-1)E_I.","binders":[],"objects":["e","a","FI","Rres","I","M","N","h","E_I","g","v","V","J","Cint","H"],"assumptions":["L1"]}],"introduces":[],"discharges":[]},{"id":"S003","text":"Let f1,f2,f3 be any three paths of finite X norm on I. For each path decompose frequencies at N/3. If all three input frequencies have modulus <=N/3, their sum has modulus <=N, so that cubic contribution vanishes after P_(>N). Multilinearity writes the remaining contribution as the sum of Cint(P_(>N/3)f1,f2,f3), Cint(P_(<=N/3)f1,P_(>N/3)f2,f3), and Cint(P_(<=N/3)f1,P_(<=N/3)f2,P_(>N/3)f3). Fourier projections contract L2 and the derivative H^(-23/14) norm. Each designated high input has H^(-23/14) norm <=C N^(-23/14) times its L2 norm. N006 therefore bounds this sum by C*h*product_j||f_j||_X+C*N^(-23/14)*product_j||f_j||_(L^infty L2), putting the negative norm on the designated high input in each summand. Instantiate this inequality for (e,g,V) and (v,v,e), where g=v-e/2. F001 gives ||e||_X<=C_M(tau^gamma+E_I), the other X norms <=C_M, and their L2 products <=C_M E_I. Consequently the two projected cubic integrals have total norm <=C_M*h*tau^gamma+C_M*(h+N^(-23/14))*E_I.","uses":["N006"],"uses_local":["F001","F002"],"objects":["M","e","v","V","I","h","tau","gamma","E_I","N","H","X","Cint","f1","f2","f3","g"],"produces":[{"id":"F003","statement":"sup_(t in I)(||P_(>N)Cint_[a,t](e,v-e/2,V)||_2/3+||P_(>N)Cint_[a,t](v,v,e)||_2/6)<=C_M*h*tau^gamma+C_M*(h+N^(-23/14))*E_I.","binders":[],"objects":["M","h","tau","gamma","E_I","N","I","a","e","v","V","Cint","H"],"assumptions":["L1"]}],"introduces":[],"discharges":[]},{"id":"S004","text":"For the forcing term in F002 use the actual stepwise Rres' from N007. On each intersected step define again f=v^n, w=v(t_n), delta_n=||f-w||_2 and q_n=tau^gamma+delta_n. On this step the forcing integral is the sum -Cint(Y_n,z_n,V)-Cint(Y_n,Y_n,V)/2-tau^(-1)integral J_s(W_n,V)ds over that intersection. N008 gives ||Y_n||_X<=C_M q_n and ||Y_n||_(L^infty H^(-p_star))<=C_M tau q_n. N006 with the negative norm on Y_n, and F001's bound on V, control each cubic term by C_M tau q_n; for the term with two Y_n use q_n<=2. N008's ||W_n||_2<=C_M tau q_n and N005's L2 bound for J control the last integral by C_M tau q_n, even on a partial step. Summing yields C_M(h+tau)(tau^gamma+E_I). Together with F002-F003 this gives sup||P_(>N)FI||_2<=C_M(h+tau)tau^gamma+C_M(h+tau+N^(-1)+N^(-p_star))E_I. Add the low-frequency estimate and F001's residual bound in the exact error identity. The result is E_I<=||e(a)|